<title>BELGIUM: Spain maize imports feature on EU grain agenda.</title>
<headline>Spain maize imports feature on EU grain agenda.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preferential maize imports into Spain will again be the focus at the European Union's cereals management committee meeting on Thursday, as all other 1996/97 grain tenders have ended, EU officials said.</p>
<p>Last week the EU approved the import of 5,500 tonnes of maize into Spain with a maximum tariff reduction of 61.17 Ecus a tonne.</p>
<p>The maize import quota, which compensates U.S. exporters for losses after Spain aligned its tariffs to higher EU levels on joining the bloc in 1986, was raised by 300,000 tonnes to 800,000 tonnes last month.</p>
<p>-Brussels newsroom +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
